OPNsense configuration download boundary
========================================

The legacy OPNsense client download_config method reads the fixed
/api/core/backup/download/this endpoint as raw XML through the existing guarded
HTTP client. It returns the original decoded XML string in config_xml, without
JSON parsing or XML reserialization. The bounded safe XML parser rejects DTDs,
entities, malformed documents, other root elements and input exceeding 16 MiB.
This parsing bound is separate from the existing HTTP response-size limits.

The adapter returns fixed failed-download diagnostics and logs no exception
traceback or response body for this operation. Cancellation still propagates;
the caller continues to own client cleanup. Other adapter operations and the
lower-level raw-text helper retain their existing contracts and logging.

The upstream OPNsense stable/26.7 BackupController serves the latest backup
from /conf/backup when no backup name is supplied. This is a device configuration
export, not evidence that FreeSDN persisted a new backup or measured live drift.
Legacy method names referring to running configuration do not establish a
separate live-state snapshot. XML validation checks safe syntax and the opnsense
root, not full configuration schema or restoration compatibility.

The isolated qualification exercises actual HTTPX clients and adapters over TLS
with a private fixture CA, synthetic XML/status responses, authentication and
caller-owned cleanup. It does not prove hardware compatibility, backup storage,
restoration, operator reauthorization or generic gateway diff/backup-trigger
honesty. Those workflows require separate qualification. No dependency, schema,
device-write or trust-policy change is made here.

